======================================================================================
  COLD-START DELAY (PREVENTS IN-RUSH ACTIVATION)
======================================================================================

   [BAT+]----[RCH] 100kΩ----+---- NODE_DELAY ----[Q1] NPN ---> DELAY_OK
                            |
                           [CDELAY] 10µF
                            |
                           GND

   DELAY_OK gates entire board:
   DELAY_OK ----[RDK]----> ENABLE_WINDOW


======================================================================================
  MULTI-SENSOR FIRE-PREVENTION MATRIX
======================================================================================

   SENSORS:
     NODE_I    (current sense)
     NODE_TH   (hotspot thermistor)
     NODE_CASE (enclosure thermistor)
     NODE_AIR  (airflow vane / thermal airflow sensor)

   COMPARATORS:
     U_I    : NODE_I    vs I_REF_MAX   → I_FAULT
     U_TH   : NODE_TH   vs T_REF_HOT   → TH_FAULT
     U_CASE : NODE_CASE vs T_REF_CASE  → CASE_FAULT
     U_AIR  : NODE_AIR  vs AIR_MIN     → AIR_FAULT

   DISCRETE OR NETWORK:
     I_FAULT ----\
                  +----> MATRIX_FAULT
     TH_FAULT ---/
     CASE_FAULT -\
                  +----> MATRIX_FAULT
     AIR_FAULT --/

   MATRIX_FAULT ----[Q2] NPN ---> FAULT_LINE


======================================================================================
  THERMAL HYSTERESIS BLOCK (AUTO-COOLDOWN LOGIC)
======================================================================================

   NODE_TH --> U_HI (trip comparator)
                IN+ = NODE_TH
                IN- = T_HIGH_REF
                → HOT_FAULT

   NODE_TH --> U_LO (reset comparator)
                IN+ = NODE_TH
                IN- = T_LOW_REF
                → COOL_OK

   HOT_FAULT ----[Q3] NPN----> HYST_SET
   COOL_OK  ----[Q4] NPN----> HYST_RESET

   SR LATCH:
     HYST_SET ----\
                   +----> HYST_LATCH_OUT
     HYST_RESET ---/

   HYST_LATCH_OUT → HYST_FAULT


======================================================================================
  MASTER SAFETY LATCH (GLOBAL FAULT MEMORY)
======================================================================================

   FAULT_LINE ----\
                   +----> MASTER_SET
   HYST_FAULT ----/

   MASTER_SET ----[Q5] NPN----> MASTER_LATCH_SET

   RESET_SW ----[Q6] NPN----> MASTER_LATCH_RESET

   CROSS-COUPLED LATCH:
     MASTER_LATCH_SET ----> QLATCH_M
     MASTER_LATCH_RESET --> QLATCH_MB

   QLATCH_M → MASTER_FAULT_OUT (HIGH = latched fault)


======================================================================================
  GLOBAL SHUTDOWN OUTPUT (FINAL BOARD OUTPUT)
======================================================================================

   GLOBAL_SHUTDOWN:
     MASTER_FAULT_OUT ----> GLOBAL_SHUTDOWN (HIGH = inhibit system)

   LED INDICATORS:
     MATRIX_FAULT      ----[RLED1]----> LED_MATRIX
     HYST_FAULT        ----[RLED2]----> LED_HYST
     MASTER_FAULT_OUT  ----[RLED3]----> LED_MASTER


======================================================================================
  TAMA ENGINE — DISCRETE MCU REPLACEMENT (BUTTON + POT LOGIC)
======================================================================================

   INPUTS:
     BTN_OP (momentary)
     POT_CTRL (10kΩ linear)

   BUTTON DEBOUNCE + LOGIC PULSE:
     [BTN_OP]----+------------------------[RPU] 10kΩ----+---- 5V
                 |                                      |
                [C1] 100nF                             [Q7] NPN
                 |                                      |
                GND                                   NODE_OP

   POTENTIOMETER ANALOG LADDER → 3-BIT OPERAND:
     [POT] top ---- 5V
     [POT] wiper --+----> NODE_ANALOG
     [POT] bottom - GND

     NODE_ANALOG --[R1]--+--[R2]--+--[R3]--+--[R4]-- GND
                          |        |        |
                         [Q8]     [Q9]     [Q10]
                          |        |        |
                        BIT0     BIT1     BIT2

   ADD / SUB SELECT:
     [SW_MODE]----[RMS] 10kΩ---- 5V
                  |
                 [Q11] NPN → NODE_MODE (HIGH = SUB)

   TWO’S COMPLEMENT FOR SUB:
     BITn ----[Q12/Q13 XOR pair]----> BITn'
     CARRY_IN = NODE_MODE

   ACCUMULATOR (4-BIT):
     BIT0' ----> [FA0] ----> [FF0] ----> ACC0
     BIT1' ----> [FA1] ----> [FF1] ----> ACC1
     BIT2' ----> [FA2] ----> [FF2] ----> ACC2
     0     ----> [FA3] ----> [FF3] ----> ACC3

   FULL ADDERS (FA0–FA3):
     SUM  = A XOR B XOR Cin
     Cout = majority(A,B,Cin)
     (Discrete XOR, AND, OR networks)

   FLIP-FLOPS (FF0–FF3):
     Master–slave latch pairs:
       [Q14/Q15] + [R14–R17]

   CLOCK:
     NODE_OP ----[RCLK] 1kΩ----> all FFx CLK inputs

   OUTPUT:
     ACC0 ----[RLED4]----> LED0
     ACC1 ----[RLED5]----> LED1
     ACC2 ----[RLED6]----> LED2
     ACC3 ----[RLED7]----> LED3

======================================================================================
  BOARD SUMMARY
======================================================================================

   • Entire safety computer + discrete MCU logic merged into one board.
   • Cold-start delay → prevents inrush activation.
   • Multi-sensor matrix → current, hotspot temp, enclosure temp, airflow.
   • Thermal hysteresis → cooldown before re-enable.
   • Master latch → prevents auto-restart after any fault.
   • Tama Engine → button + potentiometer → add/sub accumulator.
   • Fully discrete logic, no MCU, no load, no heater.

